=== entry 396b0b06eb52
kind: translation
rules: general-purpose, isolation, model-role
intent: Adversaries now run through arena's Phase A steps 3 and 4 and Phase B, whose own entries make them delegate_task children in one message, one per entry on the role line, in their own worktrees. The `generalPurpose` change is dropped (the default agent needs no field), so the count drops from four changes to three. Reading the `interrogate reviewers` line in place of `arena runners` adds that role's own default, so the fallback is interrogate's two-family panel rather than arena's. That panel stays cross-family on purpose (rule same-model-review). A T3 worktree starts from the parent's commit without uncommitted edits, and interrogate must not commit the user's work, so the copy step saves the changes as a patch the adversary applies first; no rule settles this mechanism. Keep the brief, the scope and intent handoff, and the step order.
--- upstream
